		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Re: CAT Control]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4298&amp;p=32428#p32428"><![CDATA[
The processor does remain on in low power mode when the rig is 'Off' but the problem is, as Roger pointed out, that in low power mode the USB port is disabled. So there would be no way for it to receive the command to turn back on again.<br><br>Simple CAT control would be possible if it was only to select channels, However, it would not be possible to truly turn the radio off. You would have to leave the processor running in normal mode to keep the USB port active. <br><br>Colin G4EML<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=87">G4EML</a> — Wed Aug 07, 2024 8:33 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
