		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4298&amp;p=32401#p32401"><![CDATA[
<blockquote class="uncited"><div>I'm a new user to OpenGD77 and have recently purchased an MD9600 mobile radio. I'm wondering if it would be possible to add limited CAT style control to the radio things like <br><br>Read memories<br>Write memories<br>Power on and off<br>Adjust volume [not sure the hardware allows for that].<br><br>Simple serial commands in the syle of Yaesu CAT or Kenwood CAT would be my preference with duplex serial I/O via the port.<br><br>I'd be happy to contribute to the code if CAT is theoretically possible and relatively easy to implement.<br><br>Cliff, G4PZK</div></blockquote><br>I'm not sure what you mean by Read and Write memories. The firmware uses a codeplug for its channel(s) data and VFO(s) frequency, unlike HF radios which have a number of 'memories'<br><br>The CPS reads and writes the entire codeplug to the radio in one batch, by writing to the codeplug data address ranges in the Flash memory chip.<br>After the CPS overwrites the codeplug, the radio gets rebooted so the the firmware rereads the codeplug and rebuilds its internal caches etc.<br><br><br>The volume in the Md9600 is hard wired, it can't in general be controlled by the firmware<br><br>On this radio you it would be possible to write a command function to turn the radio off, but not to turn it on. Because once it's off it is not active on usb<br><br>Overall,  I don't understand your use-case<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Sat Aug 03, 2024 10:13 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
